slug: radiation-safety-imaging-pregnancy
title: Radiation, Safety and Imaging in Pregnancy — What to Tell Patients
area: Imaging & Reports
level: Clinical
best: Final year onwards
minutes: 10
hook: Patients ask "is the X-ray safe?", and pregnant patients worry even more. Learn how doses compare, which scans use no radiation and what to say, honestly and calmly. || Mareez poochhte hain "kya X-ray mehfooz hai?", aur hamila mareez aur bhi fikr karte hain. Seekhein doses ka muqabla kaise hota hai, kaun se scans radiation istemal nahi karte aur imandari aur sukoon se kya kehna hai.
goal: By the end, you'll explain radiation dose in everyday terms, compare common scans, apply the ALARA principle, say which tests are safe in pregnancy and counsel a patient clearly. || End tak aap radiation dose rozmarra alfaz mein samjhayenge, aam scans ka muqabla karenge, ALARA usool lagayenge, batayenge ke hamal mein kaun se tests mehfooz hain aur mareez ko saaf counselling denge.

say: We are all exposed to **natural background radiation** (about 2 to 3 millisieverts, mSv, a year). Medical imaging adds to this. **Ultrasound and MRI use no ionising radiation.** A plain **X-ray of a limb or the chest is a very small dose** (a chest X-ray is about 0.02 to 0.1 mSv, a few days of background). **CT gives much more** (a chest CT is about 7 mSv). The guiding rule is **ALARA: as low as reasonably achievable**: image only when the result will change care, use the lowest dose that answers the question and prefer tests without radiation when they work equally well. || Hum sab **qudrati background radiation** (takreeban 2 se 3 millisieverts, mSv, saalana) ke saamne hain. Medical imaging us mein izafa karti hai. **Ultrasound aur MRI ionising radiation istemal nahi karte.** **Hath pair ya seene ka saada X-ray bohat chhoti dose hai** (chest X-ray takreeban 0.02 se 0.1 mSv, background ke chand din). **CT bohat zyada deta hai** (chest CT takreeban 7 mSv). Rehnuma usool **ALARA: as low as reasonably achievable** hai: imaging tab karein jab nateeja care badle, sawal ka jawab dene wali sab se kam dose istemal karein aur jab barabar kaam karein to radiation ke baghair tests ko tarjeeh dein.
analogy: Think of radiation like **sunlight**. A little each day is unavoidable and harmless; a short sunbathe adds a little more; a long day on the beach adds a lot. A limb X-ray is a minute in the shade, a chest CT is an afternoon in the sun: we only choose the afternoon when we need it. || Radiation ko **dhoop** ki tarah samjhein. Rozana thori si na-guzeer aur begarar hai; chhota sa dhoop mein baithna thora aur barhata hai; sahil par lamba din bohat barhata hai. Hath ya pair ka X-ray saaye mein ek minute hai, chest CT dhoop mein dopahar: dopahar tab chunte hain jab zaroorat ho.
steps: Counselling about imaging and radiation || Imaging aur radiation par counselling
step: Ask and check :: Ask whether the patient may be pregnant, and note previous scans and the reason for this one. In young women of childbearing age, check the possibility of pregnancy before any scan that exposes the abdomen or pelvis. || Poochhein aur check karein :: Poochhein kya mareez hamila ho sakti hai, aur pichle scans aur is scan ki wajah note karein. Bachay paida karne ki umar ki jawan khawateen mein pait ya pelvis ko expose karne wale kisi scan se pehle hamal ka imkaan check karein.
step: Put the dose in context :: Compare with background radiation: for example, a chest X-ray is about a few days of natural background, a lumbar spine X-ray is a few months, and a CT scan is a few years. Use simple comparisons and avoid frightening numbers. || Dose ko sahi nazariye mein rakhein :: Background radiation se muqabla karein: maslan chest X-ray qudrati background ke chand din, lumbar spine X-ray chand mahine, aur CT scan chand saal ke barabar hai. Saade muqable istemal karein aur daraune numbers se bachein.
step: Choose the right test :: If the question can be answered by ultrasound or MRI, offer these. If radiation is needed, it is justified when the benefit is clear, with shielding and dose settings applied by the imaging team. || Sahi test chunein :: Agar sawal ultrasound ya MRI se hal ho sakta ho to yeh dein. Radiation chahiye ho to jab faida saaf ho tab jawaaz banta hai, shielding aur dose settings imaging team lagati hai.
step: Pregnancy: urgent versus routine :: Delay routine imaging that uses radiation until after pregnancy. For urgent problems (a suspected fracture or a blood clot), the doctor chooses the safest test; an X-ray of a limb or the chest exposes the baby to a very small dose. || Hamal: urgent aur routine :: Radiation wali routine imaging hamal ke baad tak mulatvi karein. Urgent masail (mumkin fracture ya khoon ka clot) mein doctor sab se mehfooz test chunta hai; hath pair ya seene ka X-ray bachay ko bohat chhoti dose deta hai.

check: Which tests use no ionising radiation? || Kaun se tests ionising radiation istemal nahi karte?
ok: Ultrasound and MRI || Ultrasound aur MRI || Yes — they use sound and magnetic fields. || Haan — yeh awaaz aur magnetic fields istemal karte hain.
no: CT and X-ray || CT aur X-ray || These use ionising radiation. || Yeh ionising radiation istemal karte hain.
no: A bone scan with a tracer || Tracer wala bone scan || That uses a radioactive tracer. || Yeh radioactive tracer istemal karta hai.
compare: Typical doses (approximate) || Aam doses (takreeban)
head: Feature || Khasiyat ;; Approximate dose || Takreeban dose ;; Like natural background of about || Qudrati background ke takreeban barabar
row: Limb X-ray || Hath pair ka X-ray ;; Under 0.01 mSv || 0.01 mSv se kam ;; A day or less || Ek din ya kam
row: Chest X-ray || Chest X-ray ;; 0.02 to 0.1 mSv || 0.02 se 0.1 mSv ;; A few days || Chand din
row: CT head or chest || CT sar ya seena ;; 2 to 7 mSv || 2 se 7 mSv ;; About 1 to 3 years || Takreeban 1 se 3 saal
row: Ultrasound and MRI || Ultrasound aur MRI ;; None (no ionising radiation) || Koi nahi (ionising radiation nahi) ;; Not applicable || Lagu nahi
memory: **Justify, optimise, offer alternatives.** Is the scan needed? Is the dose as low as it can be? Is there an equally good test without radiation? Then explain the answer in plain words. || **Jawaaz, behtari, mutabadil.** Kya scan ki zaroorat hai? Kya dose kam se kam hai? Kya radiation ke baghair barabar achha test hai? Phir jawab saade alfaz mein samjhayein.
mistake: **Dismissing the worry, or exaggerating the risk.** Saying "it's nothing" ignores the patient's concern; saying "it could cause cancer" frightens them without context. Give the real picture: the dose is small and in proportion, and the scan is done when the information is worth it. || **Fikr ko radd karna ya khatre ko barha chadha kar batana.** "Kuch nahi" kehna mareez ki fikr nazar andaz karta hai; "cancer ho sakta hai" kehna bina nazariye ke dara deta hai. Asal tasveer dein: dose chhoti aur mutanasib hai, aur scan tab hota hai jab maloomat qeemti ho.
check: A pregnant woman needs her wrist X-ray after a fall. What should you tell her? || Hamila aurat ko girne ke baad kalai ka X-ray chahiye. Aap use kya batayenge?
ok: The dose to the baby from a wrist X-ray is extremely small, and the imaging team will take care; the fracture needs to be checked || Kalai ke X-ray se bachay ko dose bohat hi chhoti hai, aur imaging team ehtiyat karegi; fracture ka check zaroori hai || Yes — a limb X-ray is far from the abdomen and the dose to the baby is negligible. || Haan — hath ka X-ray pait se door hai aur bachay ko dose na-qabil-e-zikr hai.
no: She must refuse because radiation harms babies || Use inkar karna chahiye kyunke radiation bachon ko nuqsan deti hai || That overstates the risk. || Yeh khatre ko barha kar batata hai.
no: Nothing is ever risky in pregnancy || Hamal mein kuch bhi khatarnak nahi || Higher-dose scans of the abdomen are decided carefully. || Pait ke zyada dose wale scans ehtiyat se tay hote hain.
check: Which approach follows ALARA? || Kaun sa tareeqa ALARA ke mutabiq hai?
ok: Use the lowest dose that answers the question, and only when the result will change care || Sawal ka jawab dene wali sab se kam dose istemal karein, aur sirf tab jab nateeja care badle || Yes — avoid unnecessary and repeated scans. || Haan — ghair zaroori aur dohraye scans se bachein.
no: Repeat the X-ray to be extra sure || Mazeed yaqeen ke liye X-ray dohrayein || Extra scans add dose without need. || Ziyada scans bina zaroorat dose barhate hain.
no: Always choose a CT because it shows more || Hamesha CT chunein kyunke yeh zyada dikhata hai || It uses more radiation and is not always needed. || Yeh zyada radiation istemal karta hai aur hamesha zaroori nahi.
clinic: **Let the patient decide with the facts.** Explain the reason for the scan, its dose in everyday terms, any alternative and what happens if it is not done. Give the patient time to ask questions and record the discussion. Send them with the imaging team for the dose and shielding questions. || **Mareez ko haqaiq ke saath faisla karne dein.** Scan ki wajah, rozmarra alfaz mein dose, koi mutabadil aur na karne par kya hoga samjhayein. Mareez ko sawal ka waqt dein aur guftagu likhein. Dose aur shielding ke sawalon ke liye imaging team ke paas bhejein.
reveal: Why is the dose to a baby from a limb X-ray negligible? || Hath pair ke X-ray se bachay ko dose na-qabil-e-zikr kyun hai? || The X-ray beam is aimed at the limb and is small and well focused, and the scattered radiation that reaches the womb from a distant body part is tiny. Doses that could affect an unborn child are many hundreds of times higher than that from a limb X-ray. || X-ray ki shua hath ya pair par hoti hai aur chhoti aur markooz hoti hai, aur door ke jism ke hissay se bachadani tak pahunchne wali bikhri hui radiation bohat chhoti hai. Jin doses se anjan bachay par asar ho sakta hai woh hath pair ke X-ray se kai sau guna zyada hain.
case: A 29-year-old woman, 20 weeks pregnant, has a swollen painful calf and wants to know if the test is safe. The doctor suspects a deep vein thrombosis. || A compression ultrasound uses no radiation and is the usual first test, so the test is safe for her and her baby. || Explain the ultrasound, reassure her, and tell the doctor about the symptoms promptly because a clot needs urgent treatment. || The ultrasound confirms a clot, and she starts treatment safely in pregnancy.
safety: **Always tell the doctor and the imaging team if a patient may be pregnant,** and leave decisions about shielding and dose to them. Do not advise a pregnant patient to refuse a necessary scan without discussion with the doctor, because an untreated problem such as a clot or fracture can be more dangerous than the dose. If a patient has had many scans, report this so the doctor can review it. || **Hamesha doctor aur imaging team ko batayein agar mareez hamila ho sakti hai,** aur shielding aur dose ke faislay unhein karne dein. Hamila mareez ko doctor se baat kiye baghair zaroori scan se inkar ka mashwara na dein, kyunke be-ilaaj masla jaise clot ya fracture dose se zyada khatarnak ho sakta hai. Mareez ke bohat se scans hue hon to report karein taake doctor review kare.
summary: Ultrasound and MRI use no ionising radiation; a limb or chest X-ray is a very small dose, and CT is much higher; follow ALARA. || Ultrasound aur MRI ionising radiation istemal nahi karte; hath pair ya seene ka X-ray bohat chhoti dose hai, aur CT bohat zyada; ALARA par chalein.
summary: Compare doses to natural background radiation and avoid both dismissing and exaggerating the risk. || Dose ko qudrati background radiation se milayein aur khatre ko radd karne aur barha chadha kar batane dono se bachein.
summary: In pregnancy, delay routine radiation, prefer ultrasound or MRI, and let urgent tests go ahead when the doctor judges they are needed. || Hamal mein routine radiation mulatvi karein, ultrasound ya MRI ko tarjeeh dein, aur doctor zaroori samjhe to urgent tests hone dein.
card: What does ALARA stand for? || ALARA ka matlab kya hai? || As low as reasonably achievable. || As low as reasonably achievable.
card: Which scans use no ionising radiation? || Kaun se scans ionising radiation istemal nahi karte? || Ultrasound and MRI. || Ultrasound aur MRI.
card: Roughly how does a chest X-ray compare with background radiation? || Chest X-ray background radiation se takreeban kaise muqabil hai? || About a few days of natural background. || Qudrati background ke takreeban chand din.
card: Who decides shielding and dose? || Shielding aur dose kaun tay karta hai? || The imaging team and the doctor. || Imaging team aur doctor.
deeper: CT scans lesson || /learn/ct-scan-basics-for-physiotherapists || What CT shows and when it is used. || CT kya dikhata hai aur kab istemal hota hai.
deeper: When to image lesson || /learn/when-to-image-decision-rules || Decide who needs a scan at all. || Faisla karein kis ko scan ki zaroorat hai.
source: International Commission on Radiological Protection. Pregnancy and medical radiation. ICRP Publication 84. Ann ICRP 2000;30(1). || ICRP publication 84 pregnancy and medical radiation
source: American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists. Committee Opinion No. 723: Guidelines for diagnostic imaging during pregnancy and lactation. Obstet Gynecol 2017;130:e210-e216. || ACOG committee opinion 723 diagnostic imaging pregnancy lactation
